Clicks on a chart
The loader dispatches a phiz:rendered event with the Vega view. An Alpine handler can forward a click on a bar to the component:
&lt;div x-on:phiz:rendered="
    $event.detail.view.addEventListener('click', (e, item) =&gt;
        item?.datum?.class && $wire.select(item.datum.class))
"&gt;
    &lt;x-phiz :plot="$bars" wire:key="bars" /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

Linking in the browser
When the data is small enough to send to the page, a composition can link charts with no server request. Brushing the scatterplot filters the bar chart, and Vega-Lite recomputes the means in the browser.
use Phiz\Compose;
use Phiz\Datasets;
use Phiz\Plot;

use function Phiz\field;

$mpg = Datasets::mpg();

$plot = Compose::beside(
    Plot::of($mpg)
        -&gt;aes(x: 'displ', y: 'hwy', color: 'drv')
        -&gt;point(alpha: 0.7)
        -&gt;brush(encodings: ['x', 'y'])
        -&gt;size(300, 240),
    Plot::of($mpg)
        -&gt;aes(
            x: 'mean(hwy)',
            y: field('class', sort: '-x'),
        )
        -&gt;col(filter: ['param' =&gt; 'brush'], fill: '#4C78A8')
        -&gt;labs(x: 'Mean highway mpg', y: null)
        -&gt;size(240, 240),
);

Aggregates and time units
Shorthand also covers Vega-Lite’s aggregates and time units: 'mean(hwy)', 'count()', 'median(price)', 'year(date):O', and 'yearmonth(date)'. The aggregation runs in Vega-Lite, grouped by the other mapped fields.
use Phiz\Datasets;
use Phiz\Plot;

$plot = Plot::of(Datasets::economics())
    -&gt;aes(x: 'year(date):O', y: 'mean(psavert)')
    -&gt;col(fill: '#4C78A8')
    -&gt;labs(x: null, y: 'Mean personal savings rate (%)');

Computed fields
calc() maps an aesthetic to a field computed from a Vega expression. The expression refers to the row as datum.
use Phiz\Datasets;
use Phiz\Plot;

use function Phiz\calc;

$plot = Plot::of(Datasets::mpg())
    -&gt;aes(x: 'cty', y: calc('datum.hwy - datum.cty', as: 'gap'))
    -&gt;jitter(width: 0.3, height: 0.3, alpha: 0.5, seed: 1)
    -&gt;labs(x: 'City mpg', y: 'Highway minus city mpg');

